=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play dryrun/saved --------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: hardn's main menu on its layout, its status$
# read from the gallery's hardened Debian 13 host; its 3 the$
# real DNS screen, on another Debian 13 host; its 1, 2 and 5$
# Figma's screen mocks, under dry run after a note of what$
# origin/main does there; its 4, under dry run, origin/main's$
# Firewall screen as it prints. Nothing on this machine changes.$
$
hardn  v0.4.0              https://github.com/abbott/hardn$
$
# Debian 13 (Trixie) ###########################################$
$
  [web-01]                 192.0.2.20$
                           3 days, 5 hours, 12 minutes$
$
  [*] Risk Level           Minimal ~ hardened security$
$
  [+] User                 Configured non-root, sudo$
  [+] Firewall             Configured deny policy$
  [+] SSH Login            Configured root disallowed$
  [+] SSH Auth             Configured key-only auth$
  [+] SSH Port             Configured non-default (2230)$
  [+] AppArmor             Configured 7 profiles enforced$
  [+] Auto Updates         Configured unattended-upgrades$
  [+] DNS                  Configured 192.0.2.54, 2001:db8::54$
$
----------------------------------------------------------------$
$
  Select an option         Mode Live$
$
   1) User Management      Create, Configure (sudo, SSH keys)$
   2) SSH Login            Toggle SSH root access$
   3) DNS                  Configure Nameservers$
   4) Firewall             Configure UFW rules$
   5) Backup               Configure Hardn backup settings$
   6) Dry-Run              Simulate changes$
   7) Run All              Execute hardening operations$
   8) Environment          Configure environment variable$
   9) System Details       View system information$
  10) Logs                 View log file$
$
   0) Exit                 q to quit$
$
  > Enter selection [0-10 or q]: 6$
$
# Dry-Run Mode Settings ########################################$
$
# Dry-Run Mode Configuration -----------------------------------$
$
  [ ] Dry-run Mode         Disabled$
   -  In this mode, changes will be applied to the system.$
      Proceed with caution.$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Enable dry-run mode  Preview changes without applying them$
$
   0) Return to main menu  Keep dry-run mode disabled$
$
  > Enter selection [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
# Enable dry-run mode ##########################################$
$
# Dry-Run Mode Configuration -----------------------------------$
$
  [+] Dry-run Mode         Enabled$
$
   -  Save the configuration$
      /etc/hardn/hardn.yml$
      @@ -1,6 +1,6 @@$
       # hardn's configuration (web-01.example.net)$
       username: alice$
      -dryRun: false$
      +dryRun: true$
       nameservers:$
         - "192.0.2.54"$
         - "2001:db8::54"$
$
  Enable dry-run mode? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Save the configuration  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
# Dry-Run Mode Settings ########################################$
$
# Dry-Run Mode Configuration -----------------------------------$
$
  [+] Dry-run Mode         Enabled$
   -  In this mode, the script will preview changes without$
      applying them.$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disable dry-run mode Apply changes to the system for real$
$
   0) Return to main menu  Keep dry-run mode enabled$
$
  > Enter selection [0-1 or q]: 0$
$
